### Item Response Theory in Psychological Measurement
### This repository contains notes and explanatory material on **Item Response Theory (IRT)** This repository will contain notes and related reliability concepts commonly used in psychometrics. It is maintained by Christian Hungate as part of a broader analytics and measurement portfolio.

Item Response Theory for DICHOTOMOUS Items:
These are best understood by looking at the items graphically through Item Characteristic Curves (ICC), showing the relationship between the item response and latent trait.
The ICC will show the ability of the respondent on the x-axis and the y-axis will show the probability of obtaining accurate results.
There are three typers of models used: 2-parameter logistic (2PL), 3-parameter logistic (3PL), and the Rasch model (which provides an estimate of item difficulty only, and is the simplest of the three).

ASSUMPTIONS of Dichotomous IRT Models:
monotonicity, local independence, unidimensionality


